{"event":"answer","q":"What should I do indoors during a strong earthquake?","lang":"en","alerts":[],"retrieved":[{"id":19,"source":"kantei-jishin","score":0.0172,"cos":0.796},{"id":20,"source":"kantei-jishin","score":0.0169,"cos":0.775},{"id":18,"source":"kantei-jishin","score":0.0166,"cos":0.764}],"a":"If you are using fire for cooking or heating, put it out if you can and do not force yourself to go if you are away from the fire [1]. If there are no instructions from staff, protect your head where you are and take a safe position to brace for the shaking [2]. Open a door to secure an escape route [1].","cited":[1,2],"invalid_citations":[],"grounded":true,"admits_gap":false,"no_source":false,"ttft_ms":217,"total_ms":794,"input_tokens":479,"output_tokens":71,"tokens_per_s":121.5,"rss_mb":3980}
{"event":"answer","q":"I am near the beach and felt strong shaking. There is no tsunami warning yet. What should I do?","lang":"en","alerts":["tsunami-go-high"],"retrieved":[{"id":40,"source":"kantei-tsunami","score":0.0172,"cos":0.752},{"id":22,"source":"kantei-jishin","score":0.0169,"cos":0.73},{"id":44,"source":"kantei-tsunami","score":0.0166,"cos":0.718}],"a":"If you feel strong shaking, leave the coast as quickly as possible and evacuate to the highest place you can [1]. You should also start evacuating immediately if you see a tsunami flag at a swimming beach or near the coast [3].","cited":[1,3],"invalid_citations":[],"grounded":true,"admits_gap":false,"no_source":false,"ttft_ms":259,"total_ms":654,"input_tokens":645,"output_tokens":48,"tokens_per_s":119.3,"rss_mb":3974}
