{"event":"answer","q":"How do I treat a snake bite?","lang":"en","alerts":[],"retrieved":[{"id":178,"source":"army-atp-4-02-11","score":0.0167,"cos":0.795},{"id":177,"source":"army-atp-4-02-11","score":0.0164,"cos":0.785},{"id":179,"source":"army-atp-4-02-11","score":0.0161,"cos":0.781}],"a":"Cleanse the wound gently with mild soap and water and apply a sterile bandage over the bite [1]. Keep the bitten person still and calm while waiting for medical help to arrive [3]. It is crucial to seek medical attention immediately after a snakebite [3].","cited":[1,3],"invalid_citations":[],"grounded":true,"admits_gap":false,"no_source":false,"ttft_ms":281,"total_ms":706,"input_tokens":588,"output_tokens":53,"tokens_per_s":122.4,"rss_mb":3983}
{"event":"answer","q":"What should I pack for a day hike?","lang":"en","alerts":[],"retrieved":[{"id":127,"source":"npa-sounan-gaikyou-r07","score":0.0172,"cos":0.691},{"id":119,"source":"gov-online-yama","score":0.0169,"cos":0.683}],"a":"Prepare clothing that is easy to put on and take off to suit the temperature and weather [2]. You should also prepare shoes like climbing boots or trekking shoes suited to the mountain's climate [1, 2]. Don't forget equipment such as a hat against sun and rain, gloves, a first-aid kit, water, emergency food, and a headlamp [2].","cited":[1,2],"invalid_citations":[],"grounded":true,"admits_gap":false,"no_source":false,"ttft_ms":223,"total_ms":840,"input_tokens":558,"output_tokens":78,"tokens_per_s":124.8,"rss_mb":3983}
